# Both are optional. Leave them UNSET for the normal deployment, where the web
# app and the API are served from the same origin and the defaults
# (`/api` and `/api/ws`) do the right thing with no CORS and no configuration.
#
# That same-origin setup is what `docker compose up` runs: nginx (nginx.conf)
# serves the app and proxies /api, including the WebSocket, to the API.
#
# Set them only when the two are genuinely on different hosts — then the
# browser needs the absolute origin, and the API needs CORS_ORIGIN to allow
# this web app's origin. Vite inlines them at BUILD time: for the Docker image
# pass them as build args (`--build-arg VITE_API_URL=...`, or `args:` in
# docker-compose.yml), and add the API origin to `$api_origin` in nginx.conf
# so the Content-Security-Policy lets the page connect to it.
#
# Do NOT set these to a localhost value for a non-local deployment: the
# browser resolves `localhost` to the visitor's own machine, so the app
# fetches from the wrong computer and fails with a connection error that
# looks like the API being down.

# VITE_API_URL=https://api.exemplo.com/api
# VITE_WS_URL=wss://api.exemplo.com/api/ws
